# Ask My Docs — environment variables.
#
# Every line below is commented out on purpose. With NONE of these set the
# service runs end to end on the Python standard library alone, using the
# deterministic default providers:
#
#   embedder  = hashing      (ALGORITHMS.md §3.1)
#   reranker  = lexical-ce   (ALGORITHMS.md §5.1)
#   generator = extractive   (ALGORITHMS.md §6.1)
#
# Setting a key does not change the algorithms in ALGORITHMS.md; it swaps one
# pluggable provider for another. Only the defaults have pinned numbers.

# --- Optional provider credentials ----------------------------------------

# Enables the OpenAI embedder (text-embedding-3-small) AND the LLM generator.
# Both still pass through the same §7 citation enforcement.
# Requires: pip install -e "service[openai]"
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Enables the Cohere reranker (rerank-v3.5), which replaces lexical-ce.
# Requires: pip install -e "service[cohere]"
# COHERE_API_KEY=...

# --- Explicit provider overrides ------------------------------------------
# Each accepts "auto" (the default resolution order) or a named provider. An
# unavailable choice logs a warning and falls back to the deterministic default
# rather than failing to start.

# openai | sentence-transformers | hashing | auto
# ASKMYDOCS_EMBEDDER=hashing

# cohere | cross-encoder | lexical-ce | auto
# ASKMYDOCS_RERANKER=lexical-ce

# llm | extractive | auto
# ASKMYDOCS_GENERATOR=extractive

# --- Paths -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Directory of .md / .txt documents to index. Default: data/corpus
# ASKMYDOCS_CORPUS=data/corpus

# Where `askmydocs ingest --index` writes the persisted index.
# Default: data/index.json.gz
# ASKMYDOCS_INDEX=data/index.json.gz
